# Deploy habit

After finishing user-requested updates or bug fixes in this repo:

1. **Commit** the relevant changed files (focused commit; exclude secrets, local data dumps, `.cursor/` debug logs, `tsconfig.tsbuildinfo`, one-off classification scripts unless asked).
2. **Push** to `origin` on the current branch. GitHub `main` deploys to the Fly app `ozintel-syd` (Sydney, `ozintel.com.au`). Do this as a matter of course, without waiting to be asked again.
3. Only skip commit/push if the user explicitly says not to deploy, or if there is nothing to commit.
4. After push, briefly tell the user the Fly deploy is in progress and what to check on `ozintel.com.au` once it finishes. If the GitHub Action cannot deploy, run `flyctl deploy --remote-only --ha=false` from this repo.
